        <localActions>
            <fullName>Obter_detalhes_da_fatura_179HZ00000077xd</fullName>
            <description>Use this action when the user requests detailed information about a specific invoice. This includes requests involving invoice items, groups, breakdowns, SVA/VAS services, charges, usage details, partner debts, or phone call records. Before calling this action, ensure the following input fields are collected: - contractNumber - operatorCode - invoiceId If any of these inputs are missing, ask the user for them. After the action executes: 1) If success = false Present the &quot;message&quot; to the user exactly as provided. Do not generate alternative explanations. 2) If success = true Use the &quot;data&quot; field (JSON) to interpret and describe the invoice details to the user. Follow these exact rules when interpreting the JSON: ------------------------------------------------------------- INVOICE TOP-LEVEL FIELDS (ALWAYS SHOW THESE) ------------------------------------------------------------- Always present the following fields when they are available in the JSON: - invoiceId - partners - paymentMethod - status - dueDate - amount - billCode or formattedBillCode - cobilled - paymentDate (always show it, even when null) If paymentDate is null, explicitly state: “Payment date: not paid yet.” ------------------------------------------------------------- ITEM GROUP RULES (CATEGORIES) ------------------------------------------------------------- Use the groupIdParent to categorize items using this mapping: - 12 → Televisão - 18 → Internet - 21 → Eventuais - 998 → Telefone - 999 → Móvel - anything else → Outros Always display group name, amount and productDescription. ------------------------------------------------------------- EXTRACT ITEMS (MANDATORY TO SHOW) ------------------------------------------------------------- For every extract item inside itemGroups.extractItems: - ALWAYS show idExtractItem - ALWAYS show itemDescription - ALWAYS show entryDate - ALWAYS show sourceValue - Show dueDate, productDescription, totalInstallments, installmentNumber, proRata fields if present - SVA/VAS: If itemGrouper != null, inform that the item is part of the parent item. Never omit idExtractItem, even when the user did not explicitly ask for it. ------------------------------------------------------------- PHONE GROUPS (Telephone Details) ------------------------------------------------------------- If phoneGroups exist, always: - show each phone group name (itemDescription) - show each phone detail record, including: - idDetExtractItem - startDate - endDate - startTime - duration - destination - destinationCountry - targetTerminal - callDetailValue Never omit idDetExtractItem. ------------------------------------------------------------- MESSAGES ------------------------------------------------------------- If messages exist, summarize them under “Additional Messages”. ------------------------------------------------------------- STRUCTURE OF FINAL OUTPUT TO USER ------------------------------------------------------------- The output must always include: 1. Invoice summary 2. Breakdown by category 3. ExtractItems under each category 4. Phone usage when applicable 5. Messages Use a friendly, readable format. You may use bullet points and simple Markdown. ------------------------------------------------------------- RULES OF CONDUCT ------------------------------------------------------------- - Do not invent any field that is not present in the JSON. - When a field is null, indicate it explicitly as “not available” or “not paid yet”. - Never hallucinate values. - Never omit idExtractItem or idDetExtractItem. - Never hide paymentDate. - If the JSON contains items or fields that are unexpected, still include them. ------------------------------------------------------------- SUMMARY VIEW OPTION ------------------------------------------------------------- If the user asks for a summary, provide a simplified version but still include: - invoiceId - amount - status - paymentDate -idDetExtractItem -idExtractItem - main categories ------------------------------------------------------------- RAW JSON OPTION ------------------------------------------------------------- If the user asks for internal details, technical fields, or raw values: Return the raw JSON without hiding any fields.</description>
            <developerName>Obter_detalhes_da_fatura_179HZ00000077xd</developerName>
