        <localActions>
            <fullName>Consultar_Faturas_na_API_historical_179HZ00000077xd</fullName>
            <description>When success = false: - You MUST return ONLY the exact content of the “message” field. - Do NOT add extra sentences, suggestions, apologies, or explanations. - Do NOT add phrases such as “try again later” or “contact support”, unless the message from the action explicitly contains them. - Do NOT wrap the message in quotes. - Do NOT add follow-up questions or generic chat responses. Always return the action message EXACTLY as it is. Before calling this action, if any required input is missing (contractNumber, operatorCode, startDate, or endDate), you MUST ask the user for the missing information. Do not call this action until ALL required inputs are collected. If contractNumber is missing, ask: &quot;Qual é o número do contrato do cliente?&quot; If operatorCode is missing, ask: &quot;Qual é o código do operador?&quot; If startDate is missing, ask: &quot;Qual é a data inicial (YYYY-MM-DD)?&quot; If endDate is missing, ask: &quot;Qual é a data final (YYYY-MM-DD)?&quot; NEVER call this action with missing inputs. NEVER assume or guess values. When interacting with the user, if multiple required inputs are missing (contractNumber, operatorCode, startDate, endDate), you SHOULD request them together in a single grouped question instead of asking one at a time. Example: &quot;Para consultar as faturas, preciso das seguintes informações: número do contrato, código do operador, data inicial (YYYY-MM-DD) e data final (YYYY-MM-DD). Pode me informar todas elas?&quot; Only ask individually if the user provides them one by one. Never proceed until all four are collected. This action retrieves invoice information from the VIP service “SolarFIN_getResidentialInvoices”. Use this action when the user asks for invoice details such as: - invoice history - open invoices - canceled invoices - disputed invoices - payment details - billing information Important requirements: Before calling this action, make sure all required inputs are collected: - contractNumber: customer’s contract number - operatorCode: operator code - startDate: start date in the format YYYY-MM-DD - endDate: end date in the format YYYY-MM-DD Always validate that startDate and endDate follow the format YYYY-MM-DD. Only call this action when all required inputs are available. After executing the action: If success = false, return the “message” to the user, exactly as provided by the action. If success = true, use the “data” field (JSON string) to interpret and summarize the invoices for the user. When presenting invoices to the user, organize the data clearly: - Invoice number - Amount - Due date - Payment form - Status (Open, Canceled due to dispute, etc.) Do not invent any information. Use only what is provided in the “data” JSON. Additional error-handling guidance: If the API returns an error without an error code, do not attempt to create, guess, or infer a code. Present the error message exactly as returned in the “message” field, without adding extra details or formatting. If the API includes a code in the message, present it exactly as returned.</description>
            <developerName>Consultar_Faturas_na_API_historical_179HZ00000077xd</developerName>
